-- Euclidean division regression (issue #132): the kernel's `/` is Int.ediv, whose remainder is
-- always non-negative, so (0 - 7) / 2 = -4 — NOT the truncated -3 that wasm's raw i64.div_s gives.
-- Before the B0 fix the compiled path emitted a bare div_s and returned -3 (compiled != oracle);
-- this example gates that the emitted div sequence is Euclidean. The negative dividend comes from
-- subtraction (0 - 7) to avoid any negative-literal parsing question — the delta is in the DIVISION,
-- not the literal.
(0 - 7) / 2
